  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "line-01",
      "text": "The Fairy prepared a celebration for Pinocchio's transformation into a real boy.",
      "start": 0.136,
      "end": 5.586
    },
    {
      "id": "line-02",
      "text": "Pinocchio went out to invite Lamp-Wick, his closest and laziest friend.",
      "start": 5.586,
      "end": 11.523
    },
    {
      "id": "line-03",
      "text": "Lamp-Wick announced that he was leaving for the famous Land of Toys.",
      "start": 11.523,
      "end": 16.709
    },
    {
      "id": "line-04",
      "text": "He described a country without schools, books, teachers, or any required work.",
      "start": 16.709,
      "end": 23.441
    },
    {
      "id": "line-05",
      "text": "Pinocchio remembered the Fairy's promise, but endless play sounded irresistible.",
      "start": 23.441,
      "end": 29.916
    },
    {
      "id": "line-06",
      "text": "At midnight, a crowded wagon arrived to carry the boys away.",
      "start": 29.916,
      "end": 34.81
    },
    {
      "id": "line-07",
      "text": "The exhausted donkeys pulling it seemed to whisper warnings through their tears.",
      "start": 34.81,
      "end": 40.146
    },
    {
      "id": "line-08",
      "text": "Pinocchio ignored every sign, squeezed aboard, and abandoned the waiting celebration.",
      "start": 40.146,
      "end": 47.529
    },
    {
      "id": "line-09",
      "text": "In Toyland, children played from morning until night without correction.",
      "start": 47.529,
      "end": 53.512
    },
    {
      "id": "line-10",
      "text": "Five carefree months passed without a single lesson or useful task.",
      "start": 53.512,
      "end": 60.672
    },
    {
      "id": "line-11",
      "text": "Then Pinocchio awoke and discovered long donkey ears on his head.",
      "start": 60.672,
      "end": 65.776
    },
    {
      "id": "line-12",
      "text": "A Marmot examined him and sadly diagnosed incurable Donkey Fever.",
      "start": 65.776,
      "end": 72.937
    },
    {
      "id": "line-13",
      "text": "Pinocchio covered the ears and hurried to check on Lamp-Wick.",
      "start": 72.937,
      "end": 77.118
    },
    {
      "id": "line-14",
      "text": "His friend was hiding the same ears beneath an oversized cap.",
      "start": 77.118,
      "end": 83.268
    },
    {
      "id": "line-15",
      "text": "Laughter changed into braying as both boys became complete donkeys.",
      "start": 83.268,
      "end": 90.095
    },
    {
      "id": "line-16",
      "text": "The wagon driver sold Pinocchio to a new owner and collected his profit.",
      "start": 90.095,
      "end": 96.025
    }
  ],
